		{
			"id": "111489179555951984",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@elevatebart/111489179473954444",
			"author": {
				"name": "elevatebart",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@elevatebart",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-28T16:44:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It is the same paradox as surgeons being paid per surgery.</p><p>If you are sick, they get richer. If you are healthy, they do not. But they need to have good enough results that you still go see them.</p><p>Weird eh!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111489191164289865",
			"parentId": "111489179555951984",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/111489191164289865",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-28T16:47:30.724Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@elevatebart\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>elevatebart</span></a></span> I think the big difference is that physicians are taught from a solid ethical foundation</p><p>I’m reminded of: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/5imian/status/747817906939924482\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">twitter.com/5imian/status/7478</span><span class=\"invisible\">17906939924482</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111489200292753804",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@whynothugo/111489200177191955",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hugo 雨果",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@whynothugo",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-28T16:49:48.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Dot matrix printers are ideal for a lot of use cases (any place the prints only text, like a hospital, pharmacy receipts, etc). They’re the printing solution that makes the least money for the manufacturer, but also the most cheap, sustainable, and convenient solution.</p><p>I was surprised to see so many in China, but it really got me thinking why we don’t use them as much back home.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111489471276301715",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@nachtfunke/111489471214541054",
			"author": {
				"name": "Thomas Michael Semmler",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@nachtfunke",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/291/886/080/250/362/original/533c7d9904760762.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-28T17:58:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yes absolutely. Industrialization means dehumanization.</p><p>Big frameworks don’t want to adhere to certain standards or implement certain capabilities in order to be more compatible, because it is counter their business case. All projects that somehow depend on this will eventually crumble to the demands of capitalism, unless they remain small. Scaling is the leading difference.</p><p>Even more so, we celebrate tech projects selling to big companies as success.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111489471287271068",
			"parentId": "111489471276301715",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@nachtfunke/111489471226317662",
			"author": {
				"name": "Thomas Michael Semmler",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@nachtfunke",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/291/886/080/250/362/original/533c7d9904760762.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-28T17:58:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> and as a tribe of people were so, so close to finally talking about it publicly. Yet we are still apologists for all of it.</p><p>We are not even calling out this nonsense. These tech influencers are going about their way, corrupting even more generations of website makers, and all we do is talk about them in code, so that they never know about it.</p><p>And yet last year remix people flat out attacked their „competitors“.</p><p>(Not implying you should name anyone, just saying)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
